{
  "$comment": [
    "Copy this to .mcp.json and fill in your own token, or add the server with",
    "`claude mcp add`. Keep tokens in your environment (a gitignored .env,",
    "your shell profile, or a secret manager), never literally in this file.",
    "",
    "NEITHER provider is required to render the two example films. Both of",
    "them are pure code and cost nothing: render one before you connect",
    "anything.",
    "",
    "MUSIC AND SFX - epidemic-sound. The endpoint below is the real one; the",
    "token is yours. Setting an explicit Authorization header disables the",
    "OAuth fallback, so an expired token fails with a bare 401 and no prompt",
    "to re-auth: refresh the token rather than debugging the URL.",
    "",
    "AI FOOTAGE - Higgsfield. It is installed as a connector from",
    "higgsfield.ai rather than as a URL you type here, so follow their setup",
    "docs; this file deliberately does not guess an endpoint for it. Any",
    "provider with image references plus an image-to-video start-image",
    "contract can run the pipeline instead: the ai-cinematic-broll skill is",
    "written to be provider-agnostic, and an entry for one would take the same",
    "shape as the block below."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "epidemic-sound": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://www.epidemicsound.com/a/mcp-service/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${EPIDEMIC_SOUND_TOKEN}" }
    }
  }
}
